+ * order equally likely, and so does this — then the STREAM frames in
+ * the order they were taken, the last without its Length field
+ * (vendor/quic-go/framer.go:222-229).  ngtcp2 writes them in an order
+ * of its own: control frames of the connection, then of the streams,
+ * STREAM frames, and a DATAGRAM after all of them. |*acklen|
+ * receives the length of the ACK, after which the padding goes.
